{"paper_id": "paper-87d9d6605b1d630c", "doi": "10.1007/s44340-026-00058-x", "title": "The BIOFIRE BioThreat Panel v2.5 demonstrates comparable sensitivity on the FILMARRAY 2.0 and SPOTFIRE systems", "analysis": {"analysis": {"research_question_and_background": "Rapid and sensitive detection of biothreat agents represents a critical capability for first responders, federal agencies, and militaries around the world.", "study_design_and_population": "For nearly a decade, the BIOFIRE BioThreat Panel v2.5 has been an easy-to use, automated, “lab in a pouch” detection tool utilizing qualitative, multiplexed polymerase chain reaction (PCR) with the BIOFIRE FILMARRAY 2.0 instrument to detect biothreat agents directly from environmental samples in approximately one hour.", "methods": "The BIOFIRE BioThreat Panel v2.5 detects Marburg virus, Ravn virus, and other pathogens including toxin-encoding genes from Clostridium botulinum and Ricinus communis.", "main_results": "The BioThreat Panel v2.5 exhibited equivalent or better sensitivity on SPOTFIRE compared to FILMARRAY 2.0 for all targets, except for Yersinia pestis, which displayed reduced sensitivity due to a modified calling scheme on SPOTFIRE.", "interpretation_and_novelty": "The study demonstrates that the BioThreat Panel v2.5 can provide sensitive biothreat detection across both BIOFIRE FILMARRAY 2.0 and SPOTFIRE automated PCR instruments.", "scientific_and_public_health_significance": "The findings can inform the use of the BioThreat Panel v2.5 for sensitive and rapid detection of Marburg virus and related pathogens in field settings.", "limitations_and_evidence_strength": "The supplied evidence does not report limitations or evidence strength for the study."}, "summary_en": "This study evaluates the sensitivity of the BIOFIRE BioThreat Panel v2.5 for detecting Marburg virus and related pathogens using the FILMARRAY 2.0 and SPOTFIRE systems. The research highlights the importance of rapid and sensitive biothreat detection for first responders and federal agencies. The methods involve qualitative, multiplexed PCR using automated instruments. The main results show that the panel performs equivalently or better on SPOTFIRE compared to FILMARRAY 2.0, except for Yersinia pestis, which had reduced sensitivity due to a modified calling scheme. The interpretation emphasizes the panel's utility for detecting Marburg virus and related agents. The findings have implications for surveillance and diagnosis in field settings. The study does not report limitations or evidence strength.", "evidence_ids": {"research_question_and_background": ["A1"], "study_design_and_population": ["A2"], "methods": ["A3"], "main_results": ["A6"], "interpretation_and_novelty": ["A7"], "scientific_and_public_health_significance": ["A6"], "limitations_and_evidence_strength": ["A7"]}, "confidence": "moderate", "postprocess_audit": {"removed_duplicate_sentences": 0, "repaired_incomplete_fields": [], "evidence_replacements": [], "policy": "v10-exclusive-rhetorical-fields-1"}, "language_contract": {"policy_version": "v17.1-source-language-safe-english-1", "source_language": "en", "verified_english": true, "replacements": [], "original_evidence_preserved": false}, "status": "passed", "kind": "research", "provider": "siliconflow", "model": "Qwen/Qwen3-8B", "attempts": [{"task": "paper_research_analysis", "provider": "gemini", "model": "", "at": "2026-08-09T21:45:44+00:00", "status": "skipped", "failure_category": "authentication_failed", "error": "authentication_failed"}, {"task": "paper_research_analysis", "provider": "bigmodel", "model": "glm-4.5", "at": "2026-08-09T21:45:44+00:00", "status": "skipped", "failure_category": "model_cooldown", "error": "model is temporarily cooling down"}, {"task": "paper_research_analysis", "provider": "bigmodel", "model": "glm-4.5-air", "at": "2026-08-09T21:45:44+00:00", "status": "skipped", "failure_category": "model_cooldown", "error": "model is temporarily cooling down"}, {"task": "pa